 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "$i^*j_!$ vanishes",
 "statement": "In the situation of [lemma-openclosed-vanishing-lowerstar],\n$i^*j_!\\mathcal G=0$ for every $\\mathcal G\\in\\shv{\\et U}$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/lemma-openclosed-vanishing-lowershriek.md",
  "place": "node lemma-openclosed-vanishing-lowershriek, order 1536"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "lemma-openclosed-vanishing-lowerstar"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The point of the argument is that no section of $j_!\\mathcal G$ is computed:\n$j_!$ is a sheafification and its sections are not accessible. Instead one\nuses only adjunctions. For every $\\mathcal H\\in\\shv{\\et Z}$,\n\n$$\n\\Hom(i^*j_!\\mathcal G,\\mathcal H)\n\\cong\\Hom(j_!\\mathcal G,i_*\\mathcal H)\n\\cong\\Hom(\\mathcal G,j^*i_*\\mathcal H)=0\n$$\n\nby [lemma-openclosed-vanishing-lowerstar]. Taking\n$\\mathcal H=i^*j_!\\mathcal G$ shows that the identity of\n$i^*j_!\\mathcal G$ is zero, that is, $i^*j_!\\mathcal G=0$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-openclosed-vanishing-lowerstar"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
